    <string name="error_observed">What the app saw</string>
    <string name="error_causes">Possible causes</string>
    <string name="error_unreachable">Nothing answered at %1$s.</string>
    <string name="error_unreachable_causes">• The TV is off or in deep standby.\n• The phone is on another network (mobile data, guest Wi-Fi).\n• The IP is not the TV\'s, or it changed.</string>
    <string name="error_timeout">%1$s did not answer in time.</string>
    <string name="error_timeout_causes">• The Wi-Fi is slow or the TV is busy.\n• The IP belongs to a device that is not an Android TV.</string>
    <string name="error_rejected">The TV rejected the pairing.</string>
    <string name="error_rejected_causes">• The code window on the TV was closed or timed out.\n• Try again: the TV will show a new code.</string>
    <string name="error_wrong_pin">The TV did not accept the code.</string>
    <string name="error_wrong_pin_causes">• Try again: the TV will show a new code.</string>
    <string name="error_not_paired">The TV no longer recognizes this phone.</string>
    <string name="error_not_paired_causes">• The TV was reset or the pairing was removed from its settings.\n• Pair again: the TV will show a new code.</string>
    <string name="error_unexpected">Something answered at %1$s, but not like an Android TV.</string>
    <string name="error_unexpected_causes">• The IP belongs to another device.\n• The TV uses a different system (Samsung, LG…), which needs another connection type.</string>
    <string name="error_unknown">Unexpected error: %1$s</string>
    <string name="error_unknown_causes">• Try again. If it keeps failing, restart the TV.</string>

